WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
A new study of an ancient Martian meteorite adds fresh evidence that the planet once held liquid water across wide regions. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 239. Space-grown tumor models, new Neptune Trojans, and India's latest navigation satellite follow. With a cosmic deep dive on ghost particles, a meteorite recovered from the Sahara Desert contains minerals that form only in the presence of liquid water. Universe Today reports that the rock's chemistry matches surface conditions that persisted for

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.160
extended periods early in Martian history.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.040
Isotopic measurements indicate the water was not a brief, localized event.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.000
Ancient Martian meteorites arrive on Earth after impacts launch them from the Martian

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.020
surface into space.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:49.200
The Sahara specimen adds weight to models showing widespread liquid water rather than isolated

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.760
pockets during the planet's first billion years.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.200
The find also supports habitable environments beyond the sites already visited by rovers.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.835
Space-grown glioblastoma organoids more closely resemble human tumors than identical cultures

00:01:03.835 --> 00:01:04.635
grown on Earth.

00:01:05.075 --> 00:01:09.815
A report on Reddit describes three-dimensional structures formed in microgravity that

00:01:09.815 --> 00:01:15.455
preserve cell-to-cell interactions, Earth-based cultures often lose, building on prior orbital

00:01:15.455 --> 00:01:19.375
biology experiments that showed similar advantages for other tissue types.

00:01:20.555 --> 00:01:25.635
Microgravity removes sedimentation and convection that distorts cell layering on the ground, and

00:01:25.635 --> 00:01:29.695
And it reduces shear forces that can damage delicate cell junctions during handling.

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:35.095
That preservation lets the organoids maintain realistic gene expression patterns and native

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.895
architecture for weeks, longer than standard lab dishes allow.

00:01:39.872 --> 00:01:44.252
Growing the models aboard the International Space Station lets investigators observe how

00:01:44.252 --> 00:01:49.492
glioblastoma cells interact with surrounding stroma over extended periods that Earth cultures

00:01:49.492 --> 00:01:50.352
cannot sustain.

00:01:51.232 --> 00:01:56.312
Researchers expect the models to speed drug screening, reduce false leads, and filter out

00:01:56.312 --> 00:02:01.952
compounds that only work in simplified earth-based assays, so results translate more reliably

00:02:01.952 --> 00:02:03.032
to clinical settings.

00:02:03.612 --> 00:02:08.072
Follow-on flights are planned to expose the same models to candidate therapies while still

00:02:08.072 --> 00:02:08.552
in orbit.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:14.341
Students at Queen's University Belfast led an international team that identified new solar

00:02:14.341 --> 00:02:16.381
system bodies sharing Neptune's orbit.

00:02:16.981 --> 00:02:21.901
Universe today says the object's occupy stable Lagrange points that have remained sparsely

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:22.941
sampled until now.

00:02:23.561 --> 00:02:27.741
The discoveries help map the distribution of material left over from the giant planets

00:02:27.741 --> 00:02:28.381
migration.

00:02:29.161 --> 00:02:33.861
Orbital inclinations and sizes provide fresh constraints on the timing of Neptune's outward

00:02:33.861 --> 00:02:37.361
movement during the solar system's early dynamical rearrangement.

00:02:37.941 --> 00:02:42.481
Precise tracking of the object's paths will refine models of how the outer solar system

00:02:42.481 --> 00:02:44.121
settled into its current configuration.

00:02:44.121 --> 00:02:44.381
Operation.

00:02:44.941 --> 00:02:48.741
Follow-up observations are already scheduled with ground-based telescopes.

00:02:49.728 --> 00:02:55.588
India placed the NVS-03 navigation satellite into orbit today atop a GSLV rocket.

00:02:56.208 --> 00:03:01.748
Space.com reports the spacecraft carries upgraded atomic clocks and a new Inter-Satellite

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:02.428
link payload.

00:03:02.928 --> 00:03:07.288
It is the fourth orbital launch from Indian soil this year and strengthens the regional

00:03:07.288 --> 00:03:08.508
NAVIC constellation.

00:03:09.128 --> 00:03:14.348
The atomic clocks offer higher stability than previous NAVIC spacecraft, reducing timing

00:03:14.348 --> 00:03:16.028
errors over extended periods.

00:03:16.648 --> 00:03:21.308
The Inter-Satellite link allows data exchange between constellation members without constant

00:03:21.308 --> 00:03:25.828
ground-station contact, increasing operational resilience in remote regions.

00:03:26.568 --> 00:03:31.388
The satellite will improve positioning accuracy for civilian and military users across South

00:03:31.388 --> 00:03:31.688
Asia.

00:03:32.736 --> 00:03:37.836
The National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, issued a request for information

00:03:37.836 --> 00:03:43.316
on October 29th seeking industry ideas for boosting Hubble's orbit or performing other

00:03:43.316 --> 00:03:48.376
servicing tasks. The agency wants to extend the telescope's science lifetime before its

00:03:48.376 --> 00:03:55.496
predicted reentry in the 2033 to 2034 timeframe. A mission would need to occur by 2032 to raise

00:03:55.496 --> 00:04:00.936
the orbit meaningfully. Hubble lacks onboard propulsion, so any orbit-raising maneuver must

00:04:00.936 --> 00:04:05.936
come from an external servicer. The request covers three options, an altitude boost,

00:04:06.296 --> 00:04:13.434
a capability enhancement, or a controlled reentry. Responses are due by November 30th. Turkey plans

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:19.214
to launch a lunar orbiter in 2027 as the first of two missions. Spaceflight now reports

00:04:19.214 --> 00:04:24.174
a follow-on lander scheduled for a later flight, marking the country's entry into independent

00:04:24.174 --> 00:04:29.274
deep space exploration. The orbiter will map surface composition and test communications

00:04:29.274 --> 00:04:34.474
technologies needed for the landing attempt. The scientific payload includes spectrometers

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:40.714
for mineral identification and cameras for high-resolution imaging. Communications tests will validate

00:04:40.714 --> 00:04:45.014
relay links that future landers can use when direct-earth contact is unavailable.

00:04:45.714 --> 00:04:49.134
Both flights are designed as Turkey's first independent lunar program.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:54.049
Chapea crew will exit their habitat today after more than a year of isolation,

00:04:54.429 --> 00:04:57.849
designed to prepare teams for long-duration lunar and Mars days.

00:04:58.569 --> 00:05:01.109
NASA's scheduled live coverage of the hatch opening,

00:05:01.549 --> 00:05:03.249
and four crew members are coming out.

00:05:03.849 --> 00:05:06.729
The isolation period exceeded 378 days,

00:05:06.729 --> 00:05:10.869
studies, matching the longest previous analog missions conducted by the agency.

00:05:11.469 --> 00:05:16.309
The simulation tested habitat systems, crew dynamics, and operational procedures under

00:05:16.309 --> 00:05:17.409
Mars-like constraints.

00:05:18.049 --> 00:05:23.449
Crew performed daily science tasks, maintenance routines, and simulated surface excursions inside

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:24.489
the sealed facility.

00:05:25.149 --> 00:05:28.489
Data from the mission will inform future Artemis surface operations.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:34.422
A millimeter-scale glass chip now combines light from two separate telescopes into a single

00:05:34.422 --> 00:05:35.922
higher-resolution instrument.

00:05:35.922 --> 00:05:42.582
Researchers at Harriott-Watt University developed the Photonic Circuit, Fizz.org reports, performing

00:05:42.582 --> 00:05:47.142
beam combination on a scale of millimeters rather than the meters required by traditional

00:05:47.142 --> 00:05:48.542
optical interferometers.

00:05:49.202 --> 00:05:54.462
Early tests produced images with angular resolution previously achievable only by much larger

00:05:54.462 --> 00:05:54.802
arrays.

00:05:55.482 --> 00:06:00.702
The Photonic Circuit maintains phase stability across temperature fluctuations that would destabilize

00:06:00.702 --> 00:06:01.982
bulk optic systems.

00:06:01.982 --> 00:06:07.962
Integration with existing telescope mounts requires only minor mechanical adapters, lowering

00:06:07.962 --> 00:06:10.382
the barrier for smaller research institutions.

00:06:10.802 --> 00:06:15.342
The approach could let modest observatories reach the detail of facilities many times

00:06:15.342 --> 00:06:15.942
their size.

00:06:16.974 --> 00:06:22.634
Fermi observations from March 2026 initially recorded an unusually faint gamma ray burst.

00:06:23.274 --> 00:06:28.254
Reanalysis reported by universe today showed the event was viewed from the side, so only

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:30.234
the dimmer edges of the jet reached Earth.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:35.494
The true energy release matched roughly 1 billion years of the Sun's output concentrated

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:41.514
into a narrow beam. Side-on geometry reduces observed flux by orders of magnitude compared

00:06:41.514 --> 00:06:47.234
with on-axis detections. The delayed after-glow peaks arise from the jet's lateral expansion

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:53.034
becoming visible only after the core has decelerated. The finding explains why some bursts appear

00:06:53.034 --> 00:06:57.754
faint and demonstrates the importance of viewing angle in interpreting high energy transients.

00:06:57.754 --> 00:07:03.614
New calculations of cometary delivery of prebiotic molecules find the process would

00:07:03.614 --> 00:07:05.694
have been at best a one-off event.

00:07:06.254 --> 00:07:10.974
Cambridge researchers in a report on Reddit showed that a steady reign of organic material

00:07:10.974 --> 00:07:15.214
from comets is unlikely under realistic early solar system conditions.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:21.154
The models incorporate updated impact velocities and cometary compositions derived from recent

00:07:21.154 --> 00:07:22.374
spacecraft missions.

00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:28.254
Delivery rates drop sharply once the solar system's dynamical clearing phase ends, limiting

00:07:28.254 --> 00:07:31.054
cumulative organic input to negligible levels.

00:07:31.594 --> 00:07:36.694
The work challenges a long-standing hypothesis that commentary impacts supplied Earth's first

00:07:36.694 --> 00:07:37.954
building blocks for life.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:43.874
Alternative sources such as atmospheric chemistry or hydrothermal vents now appear more plausible.

00:07:44.656 --> 00:07:49.636
The University of Arizona launched a new forum that brings together researchers, commercial

00:07:49.636 --> 00:07:55.436
space firms and defense organizations. KG Un9 reports the initiative aims to coordinate

00:07:55.436 --> 00:08:01.476
work on satellite technologies, space situational awareness, and workforce development. Early

00:08:01.476 --> 00:08:06.996
projects will focus on regional strengths in optics and planetary science. Optics expertise

00:08:06.996 --> 00:08:12.396
at the university includes large aperture telescope design and adaptive optics systems already

00:08:12.396 --> 00:08:18.196
used on ground-based observatories. Defense partners contribute requirements for resilient satellite

00:08:18.196 --> 00:08:21.716
architectures that commercial firms can adapt for broader markets.

00:08:22.256 --> 00:08:27.056
The forum is expected to accelerate technology transfer between academia and industry.

00:08:28.079 --> 00:08:32.499
Developer Raxzerra released an open source NPM package called LaraWag

00:08:32.499 --> 00:08:38.799
that lets users build and visualize hypothetical star systems in three dimensions using 3.js.

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:44.439
A post on Reddit says the tool supports custom stellar parameters and multiple planets with

00:08:44.439 --> 00:08:49.719
adjustable orbits, it runs in standard web browsers once node dependencies are installed.

00:08:50.199 --> 00:08:54.799
The package accepts effective temperature, radius, and mass for the central star along

00:08:54.799 --> 00:08:57.219
with orbital periods and radii for planets.

00:08:57.999 --> 00:09:03.239
Integrations exist for React and Angular frameworks, allowing embedding in web applications without

00:09:03.239 --> 00:09:04.639
additional rendering engines.

00:09:05.279 --> 00:09:09.879
Plan future additions include moons and eccentric orbits for binary star systems.

00:09:09.879 --> 00:09:15.958
In brief, radio telescopes may soon help trace the origins of high-energy neutrinos that

00:09:15.958 --> 00:09:17.498
pass through Earth unnoticed.

00:09:18.078 --> 00:09:22.398
ESA leadership is exploring joint lunar projects with the United Arab Emirates.

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:28.402
A single neutrino can cross the entire diameter of Earth in a fraction of a second while interacting

00:09:28.402 --> 00:09:33.562
with almost nothing, yet the same particle can carry information from the edge of the observable

00:09:33.562 --> 00:09:36.262
universe that no other messenger survives to deliver.

00:09:36.262 --> 00:09:41.722
However, when a high-energy neutrino strikes an ice molecule in Antarctica or a water molecule

00:09:41.722 --> 00:09:46.842
in the deep ocean, it generates a cascade of secondary particles that emit a brief radio

00:09:46.842 --> 00:09:49.082
pulse traveling outward at the speed of light.

00:09:49.562 --> 00:09:54.562
Large antenna arrays listen for that pulse across thousands of cubic kilometers, turning

00:09:54.562 --> 00:09:59.882
the planet itself into a detector whose effective volume far exceeds any optical telescope ever

00:09:59.882 --> 00:10:00.182
built.

00:10:00.762 --> 00:10:05.422
One measurement already in hand shows that the highest energy neutrinos arrive from directions

00:10:05.422 --> 00:10:11.022
that do not line up with known gamma-ray sources, suggesting either undiscovered accelerators

00:10:11.022 --> 00:10:15.282
or entirely new particle physics processes operating at extreme energies.

00:10:15.882 --> 00:10:20.682
The remaining puzzle is why these arrival directions look almost uniform across the sky,

00:10:20.922 --> 00:10:27.162
even though most candidate sources, blazars, gamma-ray bursts, or star-forming galaxies, should

00:10:27.162 --> 00:10:32.442
cluster along the plane of the Milky Way, until larger radio arrays come online and deliver

00:10:32.442 --> 00:10:37.722
statistically robust sky maps, astronomers cannot decide whether the neutrinos are produced

00:10:37.722 --> 00:10:42.822
uniformly throughout cosmic time, or whether current instruments are simply tuned to the wrong

00:10:42.822 --> 00:10:49.082
wavelengths. The radio technique also sidesteps the optical opacity that hides the universe's earliest

00:10:49.082 --> 00:10:54.582
epochs, letting scientists peer back to times when the first stars and galaxies were still forming.

00:10:55.242 --> 00:10:59.262
Each detected pulse carries directional information accurate to a few degrees,

00:10:59.262 --> 00:11:04.422
energies, enough to begin cross-matching with catalogs from gamma ray and x-ray observatories.

00:11:04.782 --> 00:11:10.102
The next generation of arrays will increase sensitivity by another order of magnitude, pushing

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:14.862
the detectable energy threshold downward and revealing whether the current isotropic pattern

00:11:14.862 --> 00:11:20.382
persists at lower energies, or finally reveals clustering that matches known source populations.

00:11:21.062 --> 00:11:26.122
Until then, every new radio detection adds one more data point to a map that remains mostly

00:11:26.122 --> 00:11:26.462
blank.

00:11:26.462 --> 00:11:31.918
ground-based telescopes are already booked to track the new Neptune Trojans, and

00:11:31.918 --> 00:11:36.138
those orbits will tighten the timing of the planet's outward migration. That's

00:11:36.138 --> 00:11:40.458
fascinating frontiers for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating or review on

